{"type":"step_start","timestamp":1794253783225,"sessionID":"ses_e3e2c8327ffeEdHEddppyRWgly","part":{"id":"prt_1c1dc0093001ZarhC4e4PkzoGL","messageID":"msg_1c1dbd3e4001RI0voy014to34L","sessionID":"ses_e3e2c8327ffeEdHEddppyRWgly","type":"step-start"}}
{"type":"text","timestamp":1794253783225,"sessionID":"ses_e3e2c8327ffeEdHEddppyRWgly","part":{"id":"prt_1c1dc0097001sETheIoXGuW3EN","messageID":"msg_1c1dbd3e4001RI0voy014to34L","sessionID":"ses_e3e2c8327ffeEdHEddppyRWgly","type":"text","text":"I built the todo app: a Flask API in `backend/app.py` with SQLite storage at `./data/app.db`, and a React + TypeScript + Tailwind frontend in `frontend/src/`. The `Dockerfile` didn't need changes. I haven't built the Docker image because Docker isn't available here. I haven't opened the frontend in a browser either: there's no headless browser in this sandbox, so the screens themselves are untested.\n\n**What I checked:**\n- **API tests:** I ran a script covering registration (including duplicate names and blank fields), login with good and bad passwords, missing or invalid tokens, validation messages, the list order, paging, the priority filter, the `remaining` count, setting and clearing `completed_at`, and that another user's todo returns 404 for get, change and delete. All gave the expected results.\n- **Live server:** I started the app with gunicorn. `/api/health` returned `{\"status\": \"ok\"}`, the frontend loaded at `/` and other paths, registration returned 201, and the database file was created under `./data`.\n- **Build:** `npm ci` and `npm run build` (which now type-checks before building) succeed. I made one small change after the server test: login now returns only `{\"token\": ...}`, as the spec says. After that edit I only re-ran the type check and a Python syntax check.\n\n**Choices the spec left open:**\n- Priority is `low`, `medium` (the default) or `high`. Due dates use `YYYY-MM-DD`.\n- Usernames must be 3–50 characters with no spaces, and are not case-sensitive. Passwords must be 6–200 characters. A taken username answers 409.\n- Validation errors answer 400 with a summary plus a message per field, e.g. `{\"error\": \"...\", \"errors\": {\"title\": \"Title is required.\"}}`. The forms show these next to each field.\n- `page_size` defaults to 20 and is capped at 100. The frontend loads 10 at a time.\n- Sign-in tokens are kept until sign-out and don't expire. I added `GET /api/auth/me` and `POST /api/auth/logout` (used by the sign-out button) beyond what was asked.\n- Overdue is judged against the browser's local date. Overdue open todos get a red left border and an \"Overdue\" label.\n\n**Other changes:**\n- New frontend packages, pinned in `package.json` and the lock file: `tailwindcss` and `@tailwindcss/vite` 4.3.5, `typescript` 7.0.2, and the React type packages. The backend needed no new dependencies.\n- I added a `.gitignore` and a short section on the API and local development to `README.md`.","time":{"start":1794253783191,"end":1794253783195}}}
